#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * One-off, bounded restoration operator for the interrupted root publication.
 *
 * NOT production API, NOT a general resume/recovery framework, NOT a generation receipt.
 *
 * Default mode is a read-only dry-run. `--apply` performs exactly one audited transaction:
 *   1. restore the 15 `PUBLISHED_CANDIDATE` destinations from the pinned
 *      `publication-before` bytes (verified against the pinned proof digests), and
 *   2. move the single pinned interrupted private temporary directory into a fresh
 *      mode-0700 quarantine directory under the attempt-artifacts directory.
 *
 * It never runs the generator, never writes `.skills-lock.json`, never resets/stages Git,
 * never reads the surviving stage directory, never invents ownership, and never rolls back
 * partially applied effects.
 *
 * Invariants enforced before any effect:
 *   - physical workspace, HEAD and pinned input hashes match the constants below;
 *   - all 95 archived before-images match their recorded digests;
 *   - current destination state is exactly 15 candidate / 80 before / ledger absent;
 *   - the 15 targets have BASE-identical regular index entries;
 *   - the whole Git index listing is byte-identical to the preflight listing at the end;
 *   - the retained private temporary matches its pinned directory/payload identities.
 *
 * Evidence is always fresh and exclusive under the attempt-artifacts directory.
 * Cooperative (non-hostile-writer) protection only; no atomicity or detection claim.
 */

import fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import path from 'node:path';
import { createHash, randomBytes } from 'node:crypto';
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';

